# Rebuilding extras (phase 2) against a prefix, and running the torch-free consumer smoke.
# Hand-written (unlike requirements/openvino-*.txt, which are generated from openvino.sh).
#
# PINNING POLICY: pin what we choose, track what upstream chooses.
#
#   ninja   - ours. A build tool nothing else in the environment has an opinion about, so an exact
#             pin costs nothing and makes a silent toolchain change show up as a diff.
#   numpy   - NOT ours to pin. In the AOT jobs it is whatever torch resolves for the pinned
#             ExecuTorch tag; pinning it here would mean editing this file every time the ET pin
#             moves, and losing that race silently reintroduces the drift the pin was meant to
#             prevent. We assert presence and let the ET pin decide the version.
#
# Known and deliberate: requirements/openvino-aot.txt pulls nncf, which requires numpy<2.5.0 and so
# downgrades the numpy torch installed (observed: 2.5.2 -> 2.4.6). Leaving numpy unpinned does not
# cause that and pinning it would not fix it - only a compiled lock resolving both at once does.
ninja==1.13.0
numpy
